    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 14 with a clear focal point in **Yordan Alvarez** (73.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (65.53), who headline our offensive attack. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our most reliable anchor against Suarez; despite a neutral matchup, his elite xwOBA of .421 and favorable order placement make him a near-lock for production. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** benefits from a distinct platoon edge and a +7% park factor, driving his projection well into the \"Strong\" start tier. **Trea Turner** (64.53) also remains an essential asset; despite the dynamic platoon challenge against Suarez, his elite speed and lead-off spot make him the catalyst for our pursuit of the scarce stolen base category, even as we account for the slight volatility of facing a high-level opponent.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involves **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a score of 33.06. While **Dillon Dingler** possesses raw power, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor of **Gary Sanchez** (50.38) due to order stability and recency adjustments. **Dillon Dingler** ultimately fell below our 40.0 efficiency floor because he faces a formidable matchup against McLean (2.93 xERA), creating too much risk for our game-cap management strategy. We must also exercise caution with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (42.58); he is barely clearing our threshold today, as his matchup against Sale (2.91 xERA) is one of the most dangerous assignments on our board. We are relying on his defensive utility and speed to justify the start, but he remains our highest-risk play given the significant negative impact of the dynamic platoon split against the tough left-hander.",
